# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics was **already installed and properly configured** in this project. No code changes were necessary.

## Current Configuration

### Package Installation ✅
- Package: `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1`
- Status: Already present in `package.json` dependencies
- Installation verified: Successfully built and tested

### Framework-Specific Setup ✅
- Framework: React + Vite
- Implementation: Correctly configured in `src/App.jsx`
- Component: `<Analytics />` from `@vercel/analytics/react`

### Implementation Details
The Analytics component is properly imported and placed in the App component:

```jsx
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'

export default function App() {
  return (
    <div id="top" className="relative min-h-screen bg-void text-[#eaecf4] font-body">
      {/* ... other components ... */}
      <Analytics />
      <SpeedInsights />
    </div>
  )
}
```

This follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications exactly.

